From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wmp: control state, settings, network and controls members

Stubs (E_NOTIMPL / FIXME), as documented now. Where the player has no
engine for a value (stream statistics, markers) the answer is the one of an
idle connection / media without markers.

- Player: openState and playState follow the events the control fires
  (Undefined until something is opened), Status gives the matching text,
  close() stops, drops the media and returns to the undefined state.
  enabled, fullScreen, enableContextMenu, stretchToFit, windowlessVideo
  round-trip (defaults TRUE/FALSE/TRUE/FALSE/FALSE), uiMode takes
  invisible/none/mini/full/custom (case-insensitive, default full, anything
  else E_INVALIDARG), isRemote follows the session, isOnline the connection
  state, launchURL and openPlayer go through ShellExecute (E_INVALIDARG for an
  empty address on launchURL). get_Error returns an empty error queue object
  and get_closedCaption an object that keeps the four SAMI settings; both
  are IDispatch objects on their type information. shell32 and wininet are
  delay-loaded for the above.
- Settings: baseURL, defaultFrame, mute (applied to the audio when a graph
  exists), playCount (>= 1), rate (0 < |rate| <= 10, applied through
  IMediaSeeking), balance (-100..100, applied to the audio), the four modes
  autoRewind/loop/showFrame/shuffle (E_INVALIDARG for other names) and
  isAvailable. invokeURLs and enableErrorDialogs are plain state, no FIXME.
- Network: statistics (bandWidth, packets, reception quality, buffering
  count, bit rates, frame rates, frames skipped) are 0, sourceProtocol is
  File/HTTP/MMS/RTSP from the opened address, bufferingTime (default 5000,
  0..60000), maxBandwidth, and the per-protocol proxy settings for http, mms
  and rtsp (setting 0..3, name, port, exception list, bypass for local).
  The progress getters set their result before returning S_FALSE.
- Controls: isAvailable from the state (play, pause, stop, currentPosition,
  fastForward/fastReverse, currentItem), pause, fastForward/fastReverse
  (NS_S_WMPCORE_COMMAND_NOT_AVAILABLE without media), currentPositionString
  (mm:ss, h:mm:ss), currentMarker (0, no markers); get_currentPosition sets
  its result to 0 when idle.

